<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tanoli</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tanoli are a tribe of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hazara">Hazara</a> hills in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>, Tanawal, lies on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a>. In the 18th and 19th centuries their chiefs held the small states of Amb and Phulra, which survived under British suzerainty and joined Pakistan in 1947. Both states were abolished in 1969.</p></div>
